---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import site from "../data/site.json";
---

<Layout
  title="Privacy Policy | STLACCESS — 3D Print Scale Calculator"
  description="No accounts, no cookies, no personal data collection. Cookie-free analytics for anonymous pageview stats only. Here is the full breakdown."
>
  <article class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-6 py-20 w-full">
    <!-- Breadcrumbs -->
    <nav
      class="max-w-6xl mx-auto pt-12 pb-4 text-[10px] font-black uppercase tracking-[0.2em] text-slate-600"
      aria-label="Breadcrumb"
    >
      <a href="/" class="hover:text-[#ff6b35]">Home</a>
      <span class="mx-2 text-slate-800">/</span>
      <span class="text-slate-400" aria-current="page">Privacy Policy</span>
    </nav>

    <!-- Header -->
    <div class="mb-16">
      <h1
        class="text-4xl md:text-6xl font-bold font-heading mb-6 tracking-tight"
      >
        Privacy <span class="text-[#ff6b35]">Policy</span>
      </h1>
      <p class="text-lg text-slate-400 leading-relaxed max-w-2xl">
        I believe your STL scale data should stay exactly where it belongs: with
        you. Here is exactly how I handle your information when you use the 3D
        printing miniature scale tools.
      </p>
    </div>

    <section class="space-y-16" aria-labelledby="privacy-content">
      <!-- Key Points Grid -->
      <div class="grid grid-cols-1 md:grid-cols-3 gap-6">
        <div class="bg-slate-900/30 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/5">
          <div
            class="w-10 h-10 bg-[#ff6b35]/10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6"
          >
            <i class="fa-solid fa-user-slash text-[#ff6b35]" aria-hidden="true"
            ></i>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">No Accounts</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            I don't ask for your name, email, or any personal details to use the
            tools.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/30 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/5">
          <div
            class="w-10 h-10 bg-[#ff6b35]/10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6"
          >
            <i class="fa-solid fa-hard-drive text-[#ff6b35]" aria-hidden="true"
            ></i>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">Local Storage</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            All calculator data is generated from validated JSON files and stays
            in your browser session. Your scale conversions are never sent
            anywhere.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="bg-slate-900/30 p-8 rounded-3xl border border-white/5">
          <div
            class="w-10 h-10 bg-[#ff6b35]/10 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center mb-6"
          >
            <i class="fa-solid fa-eye-slash text-[#ff6b35]" aria-hidden="true"
            ></i>
          </div>
          <h3 class="font-bold text-white mb-2">No Tracking</h3>
          <p class="text-sm text-slate-400">
            No cookies, no banners, no personal data collection. The only
            analytics in use are basic, cookie-free pageview counts via self
            hosted web observer — no identifiable data is stored.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <!-- Detailed Sections -->
      <div
        class="prose prose-invert max-w-none space-y-12 text-slate-300"
        id="privacy-content"
      >
        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">
            1. Information I Collect & How It's Handled
          </h2>
          <p>
            When you use the calculator engines for scale conversion, everything
            runs locally on your machine. Your STL scale data never leaves your
            browser.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Website Forms:</strong> If you drop a scaling issue, feature request,
            or update suggestion using the two forms on this site, that information
            is sent to a spreadsheet on Google Sheets and backed up on my secure,
            two-factor authenticated Google Drive. These forms are set up so they
            do not collect or store any names, email addresses, or personal information.
            I keep this raw community input around only for the duration of processing
            and adjusting the conversion numbers, after which it is deleted.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Direct Emails:</strong> If you choose to send me a direct email,
            your name and the text within your message will land on my email host's
            secure servers at Proton Mail in Switzerland. Because I run this project
            entirely alone, I am the only person who will ever see or read your message.
            I keep your email active strictly while looking into your query or scaling
            issue. As soon as the matter is completely resolved, your email and its
            contents are permanently deleted.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">
            2. Cookies and Storage
          </h2>
          <p>
            STLACCESS is completely cookie-free. The only type of browser
            storage running behind the scenes is:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
            <li>
              <strong>LocalStorage:</strong> This lets the site remember your custom
              entries in the "My Library" feature — saved scale conversions for your
              tabletop miniatures. This data remains on your hardware, meaning it's
              completely locked away from me or anyone else.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">
            3. Your Data Control
          </h2>
          <p>
            Because I don't keep your personal information on any server
            database, you have complete control over your history:
          </p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
            <li>
              <strong>Portability:</strong> You can see your active numbers directly
              inside your "My Library" tab.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Wiping Info:</strong> You can completely clear your saved numbers
              instantly by clicking "Clear All" in your layout panel or by wiping
              your local browser site cache.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">
            4. Service Providers
          </h2>
          <p>I use a couple of trusted systems to keep the site functional:</p>
          <ul class="list-disc pl-6 space-y-4">
            <li>
              <strong>Cloudflare:</strong> For secure deployment, caching speeds,
              and network security.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Self hosted web observer:</strong> For anonymous, cookie-free
              event observer. No personal data, cookies, or IP addresses are stored.
              Only basic page views, referrer, browser, and broad device type: (mobile,
              tablet, desktop) are recorded.
            </li>
            <li>
              <strong>Google Workspace & Proton Mail:</strong> For parsing anonymous
              form reports and reading direct support requests securely.
            </li>
          </ul>
        </div>

        <div class="space-y-6">
          <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold text-white font-heading">
            5. Drop Me a Line
          </h2>
          <p>
            If you have an issue with privacy setups or want to check how an
            edge layout works, feel free to open a ticket directly on the GitHub
            repository. For generic use rules, check out the <a
              href="/terms"
              class="text-white border-b border-white/20 hover:text-[#ff6b35] transition-colors"
              >Terms of Service</a
            >.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>
  </article>
</Layout>
